{{/*
One release's page.

The catalog entry comes first, because it is the reason to open this
page. Cataloging a release means pasting that entry into a Cluster,
and until this page existed the only way to compute the digest was to
download the document and hash it.

Every link here is root-absolute. The website hostname class answers a
release's page at both /<version>/ and /<version>, and it sends no
redirect between them, so a relative link would resolve against the
channel's root for a reader who left the trailing slash off.
*/}}
{{template "head" .}}
<nav><a href="/">← every release</a></nav>

<h1>{{.Mark}} <span>liken {{.Version}}</span>{{if .IsLatest}} <span class="badge">latest</span>{{end}}</h1>

<h2>Catalog it</h2>

<p>Add this entry to your cluster's
<code>spec.releases.catalog</code>, then set
<code>spec.version</code> to the same version. The digest is the
sha256 of the release document's exact bytes, and the document gives
the digest of every artifact below.</p>

<pre>  - version: {{.Version}}
    digest: {{.Digest}}</pre>

<p>The <a href="https://liken.sh/docs/guides/upgrade/">upgrade
guide</a> gives the rest of the steps. See release
<a href="https://github.com/liken-sh/liken/releases/tag/v{{.Version}}">{{.Version}}
on GitHub</a>.</p>

{{if .Notes}}
<h2>What changed</h2>

{{/* The notes are prose from the channel's notes.md, shown as text.
Nothing pins them and no machine reads them, so they carry the same
trust as this page: none. The pre keeps the commit-subject lines as
lines, and the template escapes whatever they contain. */}}
<pre>{{.Notes}}</pre>
{{end}}

<h2>Artifacts</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>File</th><th>Size</th><th>sha256</th></tr>
{{range .Artifacts}}
<tr>
  <td><a href="/{{$.Version}}/{{.Name}}">{{.Name}}</a></td>
  <td class="size">{{.Human}}</td>
  <td class="digest">{{.SHA256}}</td>
</tr>
{{end}}
</table>

<p><a href="/{{.Version}}/release.yaml"><code>release.yaml</code></a>
is the document that lists them.
<a href="/{{.Version}}/LICENSES.md"><code>LICENSES.md</code></a>
carries the third-party notices{{if .HasSources}}, and
<a href="/sources/">the source mirror</a> serves the corresponding
source for the components that require it{{end}}.</p>

{{if .Components}}
<h2>What is inside</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Component</th><th>Version</th></tr>
{{range .Components}}
<tr><td>{{.Name}}</td><td>{{.Version}}</td></tr>
{{end}}
</table>
{{end}}

{{template "foot" .}}
